<p>For Gainsight alternatives, shortlist ChurnZero for repeatable customer journeys, Vitally for customer data alongside collaborative work, and Planhat for a broader customer operations platform. Custify suits teams wanting guided setup around health scores and playbooks; ClientSuccess offers packages with explicit account and licence limits. Odie, the current identity of Totango, deserves a separate look if you want customer intelligence and an agent-led workspace. This comparison covers Gainsight Customer Success, rather than Gainsight PX or community software. Choose around your account model, renewal process and data ownership, then request equivalent quotes before switching.</p>
<h2>Choose the customer workflow before the vendor</h2>
<p>A customer success platform has to connect signals to an accountable action. A dashboard showing declining usage is useful only if the right owner can decide what happens next, record the decision, and see whether the customer reached the intended outcome.</p>
<p>These six options represent different ways of doing that. Their order is a reading guide, rather than a ranking based on performance tests. Pricing and product pages were checked on October 14, 2026. Most vendors require a scoped quote, so this article does not invent annual contract totals or promise that a replacement will be cheaper.</p>
